--Description: Show the first-20 purchase records in FIFO order (earliest-to-latest within each product).
--Thinking process:
--  • PURCHASES (alias pu) contains purchase dates (“purchased”) and quantities (“qty”).
--  • Join PRODUCTS (alias p) on product_id so we can display the product’s text name.
--  • Do NOT quote the column names; leaving them unquoted lets Snowflake treat them in its
--    default, case-insensitive manner and avoids the “invalid identifier” errors that
--    appeared when we used quoted lower-case identifiers earlier.
--  • Order by product_id then purchased to obtain a First-In-First-Out sequence.
--  • LIMIT 20 keeps the output concise for quick verification.
